Direct response to real, correct feedback: none of this was actually
done despite prior phases claiming the architecture was unified. The
rail simplification was described during planning as the intended end
state and never flagged as unbuilt; Phase 6 replaced the two client-
creation wizards with one, but left the underlying "a workspace can
hold zero or many clients" data model and its full UI shell (a roster
page, an Add Client action) completely intact; and this same session's
own Phase 9 built a second, redundant "what's enabled for this client"
surface without checking the sidebar's existing Capabilities grid did
that exact job already — the precise "different menu for the same
thing" complaint this whole restructure exists to fix.

## Primary rail + secondary sidebar: one shape, not two

primary-nav.ts / primary-rail.tsx: removed the two product badges
(Showtime amber, Reputation Manager indigo) and PRODUCT_RAIL_CHILDREN
(the contextual Engagements/Analytics/Meetings-or-Incidents icon set
each badge injected) entirely. The rail is now Work / Library /
Analytics, identical for every client regardless of which workers
they're running. mobile-nav-pill.tsx's accordion mirrored the same
per-product structure and got the same fix, so mobile and desktop
navigation can't drift into two different shapes again.

secondary-sidebar.tsx / dashboard/layout.tsx / shell-layout.tsx: the
secondary sidebar used to hold SIX variants (work, settings,
showtime, reputationManager, reportsShowtime, reportsReputationManager)
chosen by which product a route belonged to — collapsed to two (work,
settings). showtime-sidebar.tsx, reputation-manager-sidebar.tsx, and
reports/reports-sidebar-section.tsx are now unrouted (left in place,
not deleted, same as Phase 6's wizard-file precedent) — their entire
reason to exist was a per-product secondary nav and a multi-client
"which client's report" picker, both gone once there's exactly one
client and one Work sidebar covering every worker across both products.

## One workspace = one client, actually enforced by the creation flow

POST /api/workspaces (backing /home/new) now calls
createMinimalEngagement in the same request that creates the
workspace — a workspace can no longer exist without its one client.
/home/new's copy changed from "set up your workspace" to "set up a new
client" to match what it actually does now.

/dashboard/engagements/new and /dashboard/reputation-manager/new (the
old per-workspace "add another client" and RM-specific creation
flows) now redirect to /home/new — creating a new client means
creating a new workspace, there's no more "add a second client to
this one" action to route to. primary-rail.tsx's profile popover lost
its "New client" link for the same reason — it was a literal duplicate
of "New workspace" right next to it.

/dashboard/engagements (the client roster + "Add your first client"
empty state) now redirects straight to the one client's own detail
page. work-sidebar.tsx's "Clients" nav link (plural, pointing at that
roster) is now "Client Profile," pointing directly at that same page.
dashboard/page.tsx's "Manage Your Clients" shortcut tile got the same
fix — direct link, singular copy. delete-client-section.tsx no longer
sends a just-deleted client to the now-redirecting roster route.

## Active Workers merged into Capabilities, not left as a duplicate

The dashboard-home "Active Workers" panel (this session's own Phase 9
work) is deleted outright — work-sidebar.tsx's Capabilities grid
already reads the same getEnabledWorkerIdsForEngagement data to answer
the identical "what's enabled for this client" question. Its
needs-attention signal (getWorkspaceWorkerOverview, also Phase 9) now
renders as a small indicator dot on the relevant Capabilities tile
instead of duplicating the whole surface.

## Verified clean

tsc: only the 5 pre-existing baseline errors (test files, unrelated).
eslint: clean on every touched file; the one pre-existing error in
mobile-nav-pill.tsx (set-state-in-effect on an untouched line) confirmed
via git-stash comparison to predate this change. Full production build
passes.

## Explicitly not done in this pass — real, flagged follow-ups

- /dashboard/modules/[skill]: still renders a per-skill roster of every
  client that has that worker — the same multi-client shape this whole
  pass removed everywhere else, just not here yet. This is what
  Capabilities' tiles and worker-card.tsx's Configure button both link
  into, so it's the next real piece: rebuilding it into one worker's
  hub page (this client's config + analytics + run history) instead of
  a roster.
- /dashboard/reports and its two per-product ReportsSidebarSection
  variants: same root problem (a client picker for a workspace that
  only ever has one client), not touched this pass.
- Deleting a client does not delete or otherwise handle the now
  client-less workspace left behind — a real, separate decision this
  pass doesn't make on the user's behalf.
- Teammates chat's create_client tool is now logically unreachable in
  normal use (every workspace already has its client from creation) but
  wasn't removed from the tool list or system prompt — untouched,
  pending a decision on whether it should be.

